bundance-and-Joy/Shirley-Blancke/9781644112168"}, {"title": "Sumak Kawsay: ¿estrategia política o filosofía de vida?", "url": "https://dspace.ups.edu.ec/handle/123456789/14860"}, {"title": "Sumak Kawsay is not Buen Vivir", "url": "https://journals.warwick.ac.uk/index.php/alternautas/article/view/1070"}, {"title": "RIGHTING IMBALANCE: Striving for Well-Being in the Andes", "url": "https://researcherslinks.com/current-issues/RIGHTING-IMBALANCE-Striving-for-Well-Being/9/26/2125"}, {"title": "Submit or Track your Manuscript LOG-IN", "url": "https://mail.researcherslinks.com/current-issues/RIGHTING-IMBALANCE-Striving-for-Well-Being/9/26/2125"}]}, "The search didn't turn up any source that directly discusses sumak kawsay in terms of \"human thought\" or a heart-mind balance. The results cover the broader concept, though.\n\n- **Meaning:** Wikipedia describes the Quechua term as a life with dignity, plenitude, balance, and harmony. It also notes that experts in the Quechua language agree that a more precise translation would be \"the plentiful life\".\n- **Relational worldview:** Catherine Allen's anthropological work on Quechua communities in Peru describes a mindset in which relationships take priority over individual agency, and collective work keeps the community in a precarious balance. Her vocabulary includes ayni (reciprocity) and animu (individuating energy), but the abstract doesn't mention heart or mind.\n- **Scholarly framing:** A Warwick journal article argues that \"Andean Philosophy\" is a sapiential manifestation of an ancient tradition and treats sumak kawsay as the expression of that Andean thought. A Spanish-language Ecuadorian paper examines whether it works as a political strategy or a philosophy of life.\n\nFor the heart-mind angle specifically, a follow-up search on Quechua or Andean concepts such as \"animu,\" \"yuyay\" (thought, understanding), or \"sonqo\" (heart) might surface more relevant sources."], "durationSeconds": 5.509030082999998, "searchCount": 1}, "tool_result_meta": [{"id": "toolu_01GTtswqXK2sK6fmmNUPRwxs", "permission_decision": {"decision": "accept", "source": "hook", "reason_type": "hook"}}]}
